ampus Life expand/collapse First-Year Experience Housing & Dining Health & Wellness Student Activities Athletics Support & Community Lakeside Living Careers & Outcomes expand/collapse Student & Alumni Stories Career Preparation & Resources Cost & Aid expand/collapse Tuition & Fees Scholarships & Calculator Financial Aid How to Apply expand/collapse Admissions Process Visit Campus Virtual Visit Transfer International Admissions Deposit Online Undergraduate expand/collapse Substitute Authorization Programs & Majors expand/collapse Academic Areas by Interest All Online Programs (A-Z) The BVU Experience expand/collapse Career Growth & Support Flexibility & Scheduling Online Student Support & Resources Technology & Tools Cost & Aid expand/collapse Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees How to Apply expand/collapse Application Process Transfer Students Strategic Partnerships Graduate expand/collapse Programs & Majors expand/collapse Graduate Programs Graduate Learning Experience expand/collapse Flexible Formats Student Support Cost & Aid expand/collapse Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Funding How to Apply expand/collapse Admissions Process Application Requirements Resources expand/collapse Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Campus Security Financial Aid Human Resources IT & Campus Tools Library Registrar Connect Alumni expand/collapse Alumni Engagement Events Giving & Impact Alumni Resources Athletics Careers & Outcomes Student & Alumni Stories Every Beaver has a story. Here are a few of them. Behind every statistic is a person — a student who found their path, an alum who built a career, a Beaver who came back to lift the next one up. Meet the people who make Buena Vista University what it is. Request Info Visit Apply Now academics Overview Undergraduate Online Graduate Meet the Beavers Meet the Beavers Real students and graduates across every college — from the sciences to education to the arts — share what BVU made possible. Exercise Science and Nursing 3+1 · Class of 2026 Hailey Darrah \"I chose BVU for the small community and it felt like home. Everyone cares for you and knows you by name. I’m not just a number at BVU. The community and university blends so well together. I’ve gotten many opportunities outside of BVU in the Storm Lake community.\" Psychology and Criminology & Criminal Justice · McKenna Whitehill '19 McKenna Whitehill \"Being a BVU Beaver is about community and friendships. The experiences I had in the classroom and through athletics taught me how to lead, collaborate, and step outside my comfort zone. Those lessons continue to shape my career as a Special Agent with the Iowa Division of Criminal Investigation.\" Business Management & Marketing · Current Junior Aedan Hayes “I love the family atmosphere that BVU brings. It makes the distance of being away from home feel so much easier!” Psychology & Spanish · Current Senior Lacie Davis “From the classroom to the court, from the campus jobs to Argentina adventures, these years shaped me in ways I’ll always carry with me. So thankful for every moment” Class of 1991 Monte Merz \"BVU is not a good place to go to blend in, it's a place to try to stand out. And that really resonated with me, and that's stuck with me my whole life, and has served me well.\"\n\n\nFounder and owner of High Country Search Group Class of 2010 Adrienne Haynes \"I believe that to whom much is given, much is required, and that was reinforced when I came to BVU. The level of involvement I had in student organizations has carried over into my career, where I'm actively involved in the business community in Kansas City.\"\n\nAttorney and civic leader in Kansas City who owns and serves as Managing Partner for SEED Law LLC. Class of 1965 Dennis Young \"I got to know all the kids. Sometimes I was kind of the borrowed parent because theirs weren't there. To have that association with them gives you a great sense of pride.\"\n\n\n\nToday, he remains deeply connected to his alma mater, funding and championing the Dennis Young Indoor Track & Field Classic each January while serving as a Steering Committee member and leading donor for BVU's Building Champions Campaign. Head Women's Basketball Coach · Class of 2002 Kylee Boettcher \"I hope people remember me as a true Beaver, someone who loved the program, loved the University, and will always support future Beavers.\" Physical Education & Special Education · Current Sophomore Guyson Lyman “Coming from a small town, I really value the culture here because you get to know everyone and always see familiar faces around campus” Write Your Own Story Apply Now 610 West 4th St. Storm Lake, IA 50588 800-383-9600 admissions@bvu.edu Buena Vista Beavers Explore BVU Undergraduate Programs Online Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Visit Campus Athletics Engage Alumni Giving Work for BVU Shop BVU Gear Tools Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Canvas Financial Aid Registrar Library Campus Map Directory Campus Safety Consumer Information Privacy Policy Terms of Use Web Accessibility Cookie Policy California Privacy Notice Cookie Settings © 2026 Buena Vista University We use cookies to run this site and, with your consent, to analyze traffic and support marketing.\n            You can accept all, reject non-essential, or choose your preferences.\n            See our Cookie Policy . Manage Reject non-essential Accept all Cookie Preferences Manage how BVU uses cookies. Necessary cookies are always on.\n            See our Cookie Policy . Strictly necessary Always on Required for the site to function and stay secure. These can't be switched off. Analytics Help us understand how the site is used so we can improve it. Marketing Used to deliver and measure relevant messages on other sites. Reject non-essential Save preferences Accept all"
